          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the previous grade we explored nets of some solids including cubes, cylinders, and cones. We saw that solids have a surface and occupy some space or volume. In this chapter, we will learn how to determine surface areas and volumes of cuboids, cylinders, cones, pyramids, and spheres, and how we can use these to solve some interesting problems."
            }
          ]
        },
